+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every registered tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` enforces that schema before calling the tool's executor. A malformed call is answered with a `ToolResponse` describing the validation failure rather than throwing, so the model can read the error and retry within the orchestrator's `maxToolRounds` budget instead of ending the turn with a transport error.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; on failure it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing required property or failed constraint without containing any offending property value, emits no log line containing that value, and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects malformed input with a ToolResponse, never invokes the executor, and never leaks offending values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L18)).
+- Valid input, including unlisted extra properties, passes through to the executor unchanged and is not coerced or defaulted, a static tool's schema is compiled once at registration rather than on every `execute` call, and a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` validates against the schema returned for that call ([validated by: passes valid input with extra properties through unchanged and validates against a dynamic schema per call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L68)).
+- `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static tool's schema at registration time and throws an error naming the tool when the schema is uncompilable ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when given an uncompilable schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L139)).
+- When the model issues a malformed tool call during `processMessage`, the orchestrator feeds the rejection `ToolResponse.result` back to the provider as the `tool_result` content so a corrected retry on the next round resolves the turn ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back to the provider so a corrected retry resolves processMessage](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L160)).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with an unregistered tool name continues to throw `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+- Validation checks `required`, declared property types, and `enum` only; it does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types, apply defaults, or validate tool output.
